      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. To make the debate competition really rigorous, I need to address the most granular level of their claims. Some advocates in these circles move past generalities and start citing specific species-level or sub-species-level differences to support a \"race realist\" framework.\n\nCould you elaborate on how they attempt to structure these arguments regarding specific racial groups? For example, how do they use specific metrics like cranial capacity or certain genetic markers to claim there is a hierarchy of development? I'm trying to pin down the exact pseudo-scientific mechanisms they employ so I don't get blindsided by their specific technical jargon during the cross-examination.",
